  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 acc. Image alone is very weak (0.208), and transformer aggregation underperforms avgpool. The critical open question is whether adding the image modality to the strongest RNA configuration can improve upon 0.591, or whether the weak image signal will dilute the RNA signal. Config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the most direct and minimal extension of the best RNA-only finding: it keeps the exact RNA/profile/aggregation settings that produced 0.591 and adds only the image branch with the simplest fusion (concat). This isolates the effect of multimodal fusion without confounding changes to encoder or aggregation. If it improves, the remaining 4 experiments can optimize fusion strategy and image encoder; if it does not, we confirm RNA-only is optimal and can spend remaining budget refining RNA-side choices."
}

